# toktopus

toktopus is a terminal-based activity and token monitor for AI coding agents. It provides real-time tracking of active context window load, subscription rate quotas, prompt caching efficiency, background agent process load, and model benchmarks across Google Antigravity, Claude Code, OpenCode, Cursor, and Codex.

```text
  _       _    _                      
 | |_ ___ | | _| |_ ___  _ __  _   _ ___ 
 | __/ _ \| |/ / __/ _ \| '_ \| | | / __|
 | || (_) |   <| || (_) | |_) | |_| \__ \
  \__\___/|_|\_\\__\___/| .__/ \__,_|___/
                        |_|              
   Universal Terminal Monitor for AI Coding Agents
```

---

## Features

* **Active Context Window Tracking**: Calculates real memory usage for the current prompt turn against model boundaries (such as the 2,000,000 token limit on Google AI Pro Plan) instead of accumulating past turns.
* **Rate Quota Monitoring**: Tracks tokens per minute (TPM) and requests per minute (RPM) against specific plan caps to prevent unexpected rate limit errors during agent loops.
* **Prompt Cache Analytics**: Computes cache hit ratios and calculates financial savings from reused prompt context.
* **Process Telemetry**: Tracks local language servers and background agent subprocesses without blocking the UI rendering loop.
* **Coding Benchmark Matrix**: Shows weekly calibrated Coding ELO, SWE-bench Verified, and throughput figures for frontier models.
* **Multi-Agent Switching**: Jump between active sessions for Antigravity, Claude Code, OpenCode, Cursor, and Codex using number hotkeys.

---

